@startuml
title POST /api/ai-agents-teams/run-on-firesky/prepare + /send — run a team whose answer is a social post
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

actor "Caller" as Caller #FFD8C2
participant "AgentsTeamsApiSdk\n.runOnFiresky(uri, prompt, replyTo?)" as SDK #D5EAF7
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "AgentsTeamsService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "F1r3node\nchain + observer" as Chain #FFE4A6
participant "F1r3sky\n(PDS)" as Firesky #FFDFC4

Caller -> SDK : runOnFiresky(agentTeamUri,\n  prompt, replyTo?)

group Phase 1 — prepare (same shape as run)
SDK -> API : POST .../run-on-firesky/prepare\n{ agents_team: uri, prompt }
API -> Domain : prepare invocation
Domain -> Domain : mint run_id (capability),\nhashes; render contract
Domain --> API : RunResp { run_id, contract, ... }
API --> SDK : PrepareResponse { response, token }
end

group Sign and send — response carries nothing
SDK -> SDK : signed = signContract(contract, privateKey)
SDK -> API : POST .../run-on-firesky/send\n{ prepare_request, prepare_response,\n  request: { contract: signed, reply_to? },\n  token }
API -> API : verify the echo hash binding
API -> Domain : deploy invocation
Domain -> Chain : deploy signed invocation
Chain --> Domain : accepted
SDK <-- API : 200, no content
SDK --> Caller : prepareResponse only\n(run_id is the observation handle)
end

group The answer arrives socially, not over HTTP
Chain -> Domain : team reaches its terminal response
Domain -> Firesky : post the terminal reply\n(threaded under reply_to when given)
Firesky --> Caller : reply appears in the thread /\nthe team account's feed
end

note over API #FFF0C7
The send response is empty by design: the
terminal reply is posted socially. Observe the
run via GET /runs/{run_id} (the run_id from
prepare) or by watching the F1r3sky thread.
reply_to threads the answer under an existing
post (parent and root refs).
end note
@enduml
